<title>GERMANY: Germans place large initial intvn rye, barley bids.</title>
<headline>Germans place large initial intvn rye, barley bids.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>German traders sought to export 116,000 tonnes of intervention rye and 240,000 tonnes of intervention barley to third countries at Thursday's EU grain export tender, grain intervention board BLE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>A BLE source stressed the volumes included duplicate bids for identical lots.</p>
<p>The European Union cereals management committee decides on the bids later today. --Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
